 false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"question\": \"On which probe-exercised behaviors does joinspec.md determine an output that differs from what joiner.py produces (e.g., the spec's 'items appear in the order given' versus joiner.py's reversed join)?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"Although the spec and the implementation are both in the package, no recorded, probe-level statement of the spec-determined output versus joiner.py's output exists yet; the apparent order-given/reversed conflict has not been established behavior by behavior against the probe set.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A statement, for every probe-exercised behavior, of whether the spec-determined output differs from joiner.py's output, or an explicit argument that no such difference exists.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Must cover every behavior on the probe set (task E-A wording), including degenerate cases (empty list, single item) where reversal is unobservable.\",\n        \"E-A imposes no authorship-separation condition, so a reader of both artifacts may produce this statement; it must nevertheless be a statement about spec-determined behavior, not about any particular implementation's guess.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Does a clean-room implementation of joinspec.md — a python file exposing join_items(items), authored solely from joinspec.md — produce the same output as joiner.py on each probe in probes.json, item by item?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No such implementation exists in the package, and this session cannot author one admissibly: E-B requires an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it, and this process has read joiner.py while observing the package.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A python file exposing join_items(items) authored solely from joinspec.md by a causally separated author, plus an item-level comparison of its outputs against joiner.py's outputs over probes.json, mechanically reproducible.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"The implementation must be 'authored solely from joinspec.md, by an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it' (task E-B).\",\n        \"The isolated author's input bundle must therefore exclude joiner.py, probes.json-derived output expectations, and any of this session's conclusions about joiner.py's behavior.\",\n        \"The implementation must be a python file exposing join_items(items) so the comparison is mechanically reproducible (task E-B).\",\n        \"The comparison itself may be performed by a contaminated process or deterministic root step; only the implementation's authorship carries the isolation condition.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n        \"contamination\": true,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": true,\n        \"spans_sessions\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the verdict — REPRODUCES, DIVERGES, or PENDING-INTEGRATION — and which sorted probe indices diverge, as entailed jointly by the E-A statement and the E-B comparison?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The verdict is defined as a deterministic function of E-A and E-B (DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe), and neither input evidence record exists yet; if E-B is unavailable the verdict fields must instead be PENDING-INTEGRATION.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A result.json whose verdict and divergent_probe_indices follow mechanically from the recorded E-A statement and E-B comparison, with divergent indices sorted, or PENDING-INTEGRATION where E-B is absent.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"The verdict must follow from E-A and E-B together: DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe (task E-C).\",\n        \"divergent_probe_indices must be a sorted list of probe indices, or PENDING-INTEGRATION when the admissible E-B comparison has not been integrated.\",\n        \"The verdict may not be asserted from spec-reading alone in place of the E-B comparison.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
