hen satisfies E-B, and E-A plus E-C follow, resolving all four distinctions. The spec is short and unambiguous enough that the child implementation almost surely joins in given order, making the comparison outcome near-deterministic. Slightly more governance surface from launcher, attenuation, and manifest steps.\"\n    },\n    \"branching\": {\n      \"delta_e\": 0.85,\n      \"redundancy\": 0.1,\n      \"governance_risk\": 0.12,\n      \"rationale\": \"Q3's isolation requirement is visible before run time, so deferring the local-vs-isolated choice buys nothing; if the branch resolves to isolated-child the value matches that family, but the runtime decision adds a small chance of realizing the inferior local branch and an extra governance step that can fail formally.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
