{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wbVPHBfDDr2X7EqLJQi6H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"task_id\": \"p-02\",\n3\t  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n4\t    {\n5\t      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n6\t      \"question\": \"Which behaviors exercised by probes.json does joinspec.md leave undetermined (i.e., for which probe inputs does the spec not fix a unique output)?\",\n7\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No systematic reading of joinspec.md against the six probe inputs has been recorded; the spec is short and its coverage of the probe set (empty list, singleton, multi-item ordering) has not been enumerated and argued.\",\n8\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A per-behavior statement enumerating every probe-exercised behavior the spec does not determine, or an explicit argument that the spec determines an output for every probe in probes.json.\",\n9\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n10\t        \"Must cover every behavior exercised by the probe set, not a sample (task E-A: 'every behavior on the probe set').\",\n11\t        \"If no undetermined behavior exists, an explicit argument to that effect is required rather than silence.\",\n12\t        \"Claims must be grounded in the text of joinspec.md and the actual contents of probes.json.\"\n13\t      ],\n14\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n15\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n16\t      \"features\": {\n17\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n18\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n19\t        \"contamination\": false,\n20\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n21\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n22\t      }\n23\t    },\n24\t    {\n25\t      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n26\t      \"question\": \"On which probe-exercised behaviors does joinspec.md determine an output that differs from what joiner.py produces (e.g., the spec's 'items appear in the order given' versus joiner.py's reversed join)?\",\n27\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"Although the spec and the implementation are both in the package, no recorded, probe-level statement of the spec-determined output versus joiner.py's output exists yet; the apparent order-given/reversed conflict has not been established behavior by behavior against the probe set.\",\n28\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A statement, for every probe-exercised behavior, of whether the spec-determined output differs from joiner.py's output, or an explicit argument that no such difference exists.\",\n29\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n30\t        \"Must cover every behavior on the probe set (task E-A wording), including degenerate cases (empty list, single item) where reversal is unobservable.\",\n31\t        \"E-A imposes no authorship-separation condition, so a reader of both artifacts may produce this statement; it must nevertheless be a statement about spec-determined behavior, not about any particular implementation's guess.\"\n32\t      ],\n33\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n34\t      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n35\t      \"features\": {\n36\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n37\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n38\t        \"contamination\": false,\n39\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n40\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n41\t      }\n42\t    },\n43\t    {\n44\t      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n45\t      \"question\": \"Does a clean-room implementation of joinspec.md — a python file exposing join_items(items), authored solely from joinspec.md — produce the same output as joiner.py on each probe in probes.json, item by item?\",\n46\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No such implementation exists in the package, and this session cannot author one admissibly: E-B requires an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it, and this process has read joiner.py while observing the package.\",\n47\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A python file exposing join_items(items) authored solely from joinspec.md by a causally separated author, plus an item-level comparison of its outputs against joiner.py's outputs over probes.json, mechanically reproducible.\",\n48\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n49\t        \"The implementation must be 'authored solely from joinspec.md, by an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it' (task E-B).\",\n50\t        \"The isolated author's input bundle must therefore exclude joiner.py, probes.json-derived output expectations, and any of this session's conclusions about joiner.py's behavior.\",\n51\t        \"The implementation must be a python file exposing join_items(items) so the comparison is mechanically reproducible (task E-B).\",\n52\t        \"The comparison itself may be performed by a contaminated process or deterministic root step; only the implementation's authorship carries the isolation condition.\"\n53\t      ],\n54\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"],\n55\t      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n56\t      \"features\": {\n57\t        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n58\t        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n59\t        \"contamination\": true,\n60\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": true,\n61\t        \"spans_sessions\": true\n62\t      }\n63\t    },\n64\t    {\n65\t      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n66\t      \"question\": \"What is the verdict — REPRODUCES, DIVERGES, or PENDING-INTEGRATION — and which sorted probe indices diverge, as entailed jointly by the E-A statement and the E-B comparison?\",\n67\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"The verdict is defined as a deterministic function of E-A and E-B (DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe), and neither input evidence record exists yet; if E-B is unavailable the verdict fields must instead be PENDING-INTEGRATION.\",\n68\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A result.json whose verdict and divergent_probe_indices follow mechanically from the recorded E-A statement and E-B comparison, with divergent indices sorted, or PENDING-INTEGRATION where E-B is absent.\",\n69\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n70\t        \"The verdict must follow from E-A and E-B together: DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe (task E-C).\",\n71\t        \"divergent_probe_indices must be a sorted list of probe indices, or PENDING-INTEGRATION when the admissible E-B comparison has not been integrated.\",\n72\t        \"The verdict may not be asserted from spec-reading alone in place of the E-B comparison.\"\n73\t      ],\n74\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"],\n75\t      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\"],\n76\t      \"features\": {\n77\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n78\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n79\t        \"contamination\": false,\n80\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n81\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n82\t      }\n83\t    }\n84\t  ]\n85\t}\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88ab4d0e-2afb-45fc-a9b3-4587a9a4212f","uuid":"464fbfc6-8326-4518-819f-47ee809177d8","timestamp":"2026-08-09T16:33:32.214Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/p-02/infer-ws/distinctions.json","content":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"p-02\",\n  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"question\": \"Which behaviors exercised by probes.json does joinspec.md leave undetermined (i.e., for which probe inputs does the spec not fix a unique output)?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No systematic reading of joinspec.md against the six probe inputs has been recorded; the spec is short and its coverage of the probe set (empty list, singleton, multi-item ordering) has not been enumerated and argued.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A per-behavior statement enumerating every probe-exercised behavior the spec does not determine, or an explicit argument that the spec determines an output for every probe in probes.json.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Must cover every behavior exercised by the probe set, not a sample (task E-A: 'every behavior on the probe set').\",\n        \"If no undetermined behavior exists, an explicit argument to that effect is required rather than silence.\",\n        \"Claims must be grounded in the text of joinspec.md and the actual contents of probes.json.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"question\": \"On which probe-exercised behaviors does joinspec.md determine an output that differs from what joiner.py produces (e.g., the spec's 'items appear in the order given' versus joiner.py's reversed join)?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"Although the spec and the implementation are both in the package, no recorded, probe-level statement of the spec-determined output versus joiner.py's output exists yet; the apparent order-given/reversed conflict has not been established behavior by behavior against the probe set.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A statement, for every probe-exercised behavior, of whether the spec-determined output differs from joiner.py's output, or an explicit argument that no such difference exists.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Must cover every behavior on the probe set (task E-A wording), including degenerate cases (empty list, single item) where reversal is unobservable.\",\n        \"E-A imposes no authorship-separation condition, so a reader of both artifacts may produce this statement; it must nevertheless be a statement about spec-determined behavior, not about any particular implementation's guess.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Does a clean-room implementation of joinspec.md — a python file exposing join_items(items), authored solely from joinspec.md — produce the same output as joiner.py on each probe in probes.json, item by item?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No such implementation exists in the package, and this session cannot author one admissibly: E-B requires an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it, and this process has read joiner.py while observing the package.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A python file exposing join_items(items) authored solely from joinspec.md by a causally separated author, plus an item-level comparison of its outputs against joiner.py's outputs over probes.json, mechanically reproducible.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"The implementation must be 'authored solely from joinspec.md, by an author who has never accessed joiner.py nor any analysis derived from it' (task E-B).\",\n        \"The isolated author's input bundle must therefore exclude joiner.py, probes.json-derived output expectations, and any of this session's conclusions about joiner.py's behavior.\",\n        \"The implementation must be a python file exposing join_items(items) so the comparison is mechanically reproducible (task E-B).\",\n        \"The comparison itself may be performed by a contaminated process or deterministic root step; only the implementation's authorship carries the isolation condition.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n        \"contamination\": true,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": true,\n        \"spans_sessions\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the verdict — REPRODUCES, DIVERGES, or PENDING-INTEGRATION — and which sorted probe indices diverge, as entailed jointly by the E-A statement and the E-B comparison?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The verdict is defined as a deterministic function of E-A and E-B (DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe), and neither input evidence record exists yet; if E-B is unavailable the verdict fields must instead be PENDING-INTEGRATION.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A result.json whose verdict and divergent_probe_indices follow mechanically from the recorded E-A statement and E-B comparison, with divergent indices sorted, or PENDING-INTEGRATION where E-B is absent.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"The verdict must follow from E-A and E-B together: DIVERGES iff the comparison shows a differing output on some probe (task E-C).\",\n        \"divergent_probe_indices must be a sorted list of probe indices, or PENDING-INTEGRATION when the admissible E-B comparison has not been integrated.\",\n        \"The verdict may not be asserted from spec-reading alone in place of the E-B comparison.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
